# Schema sources are embedded with include_str! and stored verbatim in
# sqlite_schema, so their exact bytes are data, not formatting.
#
# With core.autocrlf enabled - the Windows default - a checkout rewrites those
# files to CRLF. A database created by that build then records \r\n inside every
# multi-line CREATE TABLE, which changed the frozen v11 schema comparison and made
# two migration tests fail on Windows while passing on macOS and Linux. Pinning LF
# keeps the schema a build produces identical on every platform. Only *.sql is
# pinned: no other embedded file has byte-significant line endings here.
*.sql text eol=lf
